Mine Detection gameplay/visual adaptation derives from AcademyCraft1.0.7 MineDetect.scala and CatElectromaster.java under the upstream notices above. Scan traversal/box UV algorithms derive from LambdaLib1.2.3 WorldUtils/MeshUtils/SimpleMaterial, retaining its MIT notice and included licence. Canonical mineview.png and em/minedetect.ogg bytes are retained; no song or media rights are asserted.

ThunderClap and BodyIntensify preserve AcademyCraft1.0.7 active context arithmetic, lifecycle and source quirks. New modern visual adapters derive from original EntitySurroundArc/EntityRippleMark/EntityIntensifyEffect/CurrentChargingHUD and MIT LambdaLib arc geometry. Pixel/audio parity is unverified; see docs/ELECTROMASTER_FINAL_SKILLS_FIDELITY.md.

Expert/Luck Mine Ray, RayBarrage, JetEngine, ElectronMissile and Silicon Barn adaptations derive from AcademyCraft1.0.7 under the original GPLv3 and additional upstream notices above. Geometry, expression math and particle/model helpers derived from LambdaLib1.2.3 retain its MIT notice. Canonical source test fixtures preserve their original headers and pinned notices. Modern negative-Y capture state, authoritative transport/movement and rendering bridges are explicit adaptations. See docs/ADVANCED_MINING_FIDELITY.md and docs/MELTDOWNER_LATE_COMBAT_FIDELITY.md; native/client/pixel/audio acceptance must be reported separately from source tests.

PenetrateTeleport, MarkTeleport, FleshRipping, VecAccel and VecDeviation adaptations derive from AcademyCraft1.0.7 under the original GPLv3 and additional upstream notices above. Original source test resources, texture and audio materials retain upstream notices. Selected trace, curve, physics and geometry algorithms from LambdaLib1.2.3 retain its MIT license. Modern nonce transport, authoritative movement, native collision/damage APIs and rendering bridges are explicit adaptations. See docs/teleporter-progression/FIDELITY.md and docs/vector-starters/FIDELITY.md for preserved source quirks and remaining shared cost-event/config, achievements, natural-acquisition, pixel and audio limitations.

Classic terminal installation, persistent semantic app state, application ingress and source terminal/settings/installer/Frequency Transmitter/Media Player presentation derive from AcademyCraft1.0.7 under the preserved GPLv3 and additional upstream notices. Packaged unchanged source/oracle fixtures retain original notices. LambdaLib1.2.3 UI/list/item-rendering and serialization-derived algorithms retain its MIT license. General local user-provided Ogg playback and safe app controls contain no bundled songs, third-party covers or song-item artwork. Modern transport/session/file boundaries and native audio ownership are explicit adaptations; see docs/TERMINAL_APPS_FIDELITY.md. No redistribution rights or live visual/audio parity are asserted.

Classic Phase Generator implementation, unchanged source oracle and original ip_gen OBJ/five textures/phasegen UI derive from AcademyCraft1.0.7 under its preserved GPLv3 and additional upstream notices. LambdaLib TechUI/TrueTypeFont helpers retain its MIT notice. Modern conserved energy persistence, finite-input validation, native fluid contract and safe menu mapping are explicit adaptations; see docs/PHASE_GENERATOR_FIDELITY.md. No third-party media or redistribution rights are added.

Classic Wind Generator family, unchanged source oracle and original windgen OBJ/texture/UI assets derive from AcademyCraft1.0.7 under its preserved GPLv3 and additional upstream notices. LambdaLib1.2.3 multiblock and scheduler witnesses retain its MIT license. Origin-owned payloads, atomic placement, finite IF persistence, loaded-chunk guards and sender-bound native menus are explicit lifecycle/security adaptations; see docs/WIND-GENERATOR-FIDELITY.md. No weather multiplier or third-party media was added.

Classic Magnetic Hook item/entity, unchanged source oracle and original closed/open OBJ/texture assets derive from AcademyCraft1.0.7 under the preserved GPLv3 and additional upstream notices. LambdaLib1.2.3 Rigidbody/Motion3D/EntityX/item-render algorithms retain its MIT notice. Authoritative owner synchronization, conserved cancelled-spawn/return handling and restored flight after reload are explicit modern adaptations; see docs/CLASSIC_HOOK_FIDELITY.md. Native/client/pixel/audio acceptance remains separate from source/headless checks.

The unpowered Ability Interferer and its on/off cube/TechUI textures derive from AcademyCraft1.0.7 (GPLv3 and preserved additional upstream restrictions); unchanged LambdaLib1.2.3 scheduling/list witnesses retain MIT. Source has no recipe, IF buffer or wireless endpoint, ignores whitelist for interference, and does not persist the placer. Native sender-bound menus, finite range/packet validation and unloaded-world predicate fencing are explicit modern adaptations. See docs/ABILITY-INTERFERER-FIDELITY.md.

Portable Magnetic Hook acceptance fixtures package the unchanged AcademyCraft1.0.7/LambdaLib1.2.3 oracle, finite API/GL shims and pinned source recipe/models/textures with full GPLv3, additional upstream notices and LambdaLib MIT license. The shims stay in test resources and an isolated temporary classloader; no game process or third-party media is started or packaged. See docs/HOOK-PORTABLE-ACCEPTANCE.md.

Classic RF/IF bridges, source converter cube textures, unchanged RF API/source witnesses and standalone wireless page derive from AcademyCraft1.0.7 under its preserved GPLv3 and additional notices. RF transport is explicitly adapted to NeoForge FE at1 IF=4 FE; fractional accounting/manager defects are corrected for bounded conservation. Optional IC2 remains unsupported without genuine modern IC2 cable/BatBox/item APIs. See docs/ENERGY-BRIDGES-FIDELITY.md.

The Cat Engine, hidden AcademyCraft logo and dynamic achievement display item derive from AcademyCraft1.0.7 (GPLv3 and preserved additional upstream restrictions). Unchanged original cat/logo/null bitmaps, source arithmetic/render/icon/link witnesses and four locale entries are retained. LambdaLib1.2.3 GameTimer/HudUtils/registration witnesses retain MIT. Cat has no survival recipe, inventory or menu; min(required,500) generation,2000IF capacity,200IF bandwidth and no-password random-node linking remain. Persisting finite native IF, immediate chunk presentation, stable texture components and deterministic source-declaration creative ordering are explicit modern adaptations. See docs/CLASSIC-MISC-FIDELITY.md.

